meta {
  name: 1. Start Checkout
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/suscripciones
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{jwt}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "ciclo": "mensual",
    "facturacion": {
      "nombreCompleto": "Demo User",
      "email": "generic.user@gmail.com",
      "pais": "MX",
      "ciudad": "CDMX",
      "direccion": "Calle 1 #123",
      "codigoPostal": "06600"
    }
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.suscripcionId) {
    bru.setVar("suscripcionId", res.body.suscripcionId);
  }
  if (res.body && res.body.clientSecret) {
    bru.setVar("clientSecret", res.body.clientSecret);
  }
}

docs {
  Step one of two. Returns a Stripe clientSecret and publishableKey. Requires
  STRIPE_SECRET_KEY / STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_* to be configured (Stripe test mode) — otherwise
  this call fails.

  Safe to re-run: an existing INCOMPLETA subscription for the same cycle is reused rather
  than duplicated in Stripe, so retrying after a back-button never creates a second row.

  Bruno cannot complete step two by itself: confirming the payment requires Stripe
  Elements tokenizing a card client-side in a browser (by design — the server never
  touches raw card numbers). Use the live checkout at the frontend URL with Stripe's test
  card 4242 4242 4242 4242 / any future date / any CVC, then call "2. Confirm Payment"
  below with the suscripcionId it produces.
}
